{"name":"Minerva","hex":"#b5deda","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Minerva","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The goddess of wisdom, especially strategic warfare, and the arts, especially crafts and in particular weaving. She is the Roman counterpart of Athena.","93 Minerva, a main belt asteroid."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Minerva"}],"entries":[{"title":"Minerva","blocks":[{"text":"Minerva is the Roman goddess of wisdom, justice, law, victory, and the sponsor of arts, trade, and strategy. She is also a goddess of warfare, though with a focus on strategic warfare, rather than the violence of gods such as Mars. Beginning in the second century BC, the Romans equated her with the Greek goddess Athena. Minerva is one of the three Roman deities in the Capitoline Triad, along with Jupiter and Juno."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Herculaneum_Collegio_degli_Augustali_Ercole_sull%27Olimpo_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Herculaneum_Collegio_degli_Augustali_Ercole_sull%27Olimpo_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minerva","wikidata":"Q126916"},{"title":"Minerva (automobile)","blocks":[{"text":"Minerva was a Belgian business that made in bicycles, motorcycles, and later automobiles, between 1897 and 1958."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/Minerva_logo.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minerva_(automobile)","wikidata":"Q1814703"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/500px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikim